  <running_head>De Etymologia</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">ab Indefinito secundo indicativo. ut:</l>
    <l n="2">ἐτύπτεσε, τυπτέσθην : ἔθεσε, θέσθην.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Futurum primum</i>, à Futuri primi in-</l>
    <l n="4">dicativi persona secunda plurali: ε in</l>
    <l n="5">αι mutando. ut: τύψεσθε, τύψεσθην:</l>
    <l n="6">ποιήσεσθε, ποιήσεσθην</l>
    <l n="7">: θήσεσθε, θήσεσθην.</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Futurum secundum</i>, eodem modo, à</l>
    <l n="9">Futuri secundi indicativi persona</l>
    <l n="10">secunda plurali. ut: τυπτεῖσθε, τυπτεῖσθην.</l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="1" para="true">DE VERBIS ANOMALIS</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="1">&amp; Defectivis.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Rara sunt Verba apud Græcos, quæ</l>
    <l n="14">omnia sua tempora analogicè, &amp;</l>
    <l n="15">secundùm præscriptas Conjugationum</l>
    <l n="16">regulas, formant; nec ab aliquo alio</l>
    <l n="17">themate tempora quædam mutuentur.</l>
    <l n="18">Hinc <i>Verba anomala</i> seu irregularia di-</l>
    <l n="19">cta, &amp; <i>defectiva</i>.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Sunt autem defectiva verba, quæ</l>
    <l n="21">temporibus quibusdam regulariter</l>
    <l n="22">formatis deficiunt.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Atque horum pleraque omnia, ultra</l>
    <l n="24">Imperfectū, regulariter non conjugan-</l>
    <l n="25">tur: &amp;, si quę præterea tempora habent,</l>
    <l n="26">illa ab alio themate, plerunque inusita-</l>
    <l n="27">to, mutuantur.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">Talia</l>
  </main_text>
